**Describe the bug**

Opening a package **by file path** with `isEditable: false` (read-only) can modify the file on disk. When a relationship has an external target that `Uri.TryCreate` rejects (for example a `mailto:` hyperlink with several recipients on .NET 8), the original target is replaced by `rewritten://<GUID>` **in the file itself**, and it is never restored. Nothing is saved or edited by the caller; reading is enough.

Opening the same file through a read-only `FileStream` leaves it untouched, which is the behavior I'd expect from both.

**To Reproduce**

Console app (net8.0, `DocumentFormat.OpenXml` 3.5.1). It creates a workbook with a hyperlink to `mailto:a@a.com;b@b.com`, opens it read-only by path, reads one thing, disposes, and compares the file.

```csharp
using System.IO.Compression;
using System.Text;
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml;
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Packaging;
using DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Spreadsheet;

// A hyperlink target that Uri.TryCreate rejects on .NET 8 (several recipients).
const string Target = "mailto:a@a.com;b@b.com";
const string RelsPath = "xl/worksheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels";

var path = Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), "multi-recipient-mailto.xlsx");
CreateWorkbookWithHyperlink(path);

Console.WriteLine($"Before: {ReadTarget(path)}");

var before = File.ReadAllBytes(path);
var writeTime = File.GetLastWriteTimeUtc(path);

// Open for reading only, read something, dispose. No edits, no Save.
using (var doc = SpreadsheetDocument.Open(path, isEditable: false))
{
    _ = doc.WorkbookPart!.WorksheetParts.First().Worksheet.InnerXml;
}

Console.WriteLine($"After : {ReadTarget(path)}");
Console.WriteLine($"File bytes changed: {!before.AsSpan().SequenceEqual(File.ReadAllBytes(path))}");
Console.WriteLine($"Write time changed: {File.GetLastWriteTimeUtc(path) != writeTime}");

// Same file through a read-only stream: untouched.
CreateWorkbookWithHyperlink(path);
using (var fs = new FileStream(path, FileMode.Open, FileAccess.Read, FileShare.Read))
using (var doc = SpreadsheetDocument.Open(fs, isEditable: false))
{
    _ = doc.WorkbookPart!.WorksheetParts.First().Worksheet.InnerXml;
}
Console.WriteLine($"Via read-only FileStream: {ReadTarget(path)}");

static void CreateWorkbookWithHyperlink(string path)
{
    using (var doc = SpreadsheetDocument.Create(path, SpreadsheetDocumentType.Workbook))
    {
        var workbookPart = doc.AddWorkbookPart();
        workbookPart.Workbook = new Workbook(new Sheets());
        var sheetPart = workbookPart.AddNewPart<WorksheetPart>();
        var rel = sheetPart.AddHyperlinkRelationship(new Uri("mailto:placeholder@a.com"), true);
        sheetPart.Worksheet = new Worksheet(
            new SheetData(new Row(new Cell { CellReference = "A1", DataType = CellValues.String, CellValue = new CellValue("mail") }) { RowIndex = 1 }),
            new Hyperlinks(new Hyperlink { Reference = "A1", Id = rel.Id }));
        workbookPart.Workbook.Sheets!.Append(new Sheet { Id = workbookPart.GetIdOfPart(sheetPart), SheetId = 1, Name = "Sheet1" });
    }

    // Excel stores the address as typed; the SDK would reject it on write, so patch the .rels part.
    using var zip = ZipFile.Open(path, ZipArchiveMode.Update);
    var entry = zip.GetEntry(RelsPath)!;
    string xml;
    using (var reader = new StreamReader(entry.Open())) xml = reader.ReadToEnd();
    entry.Delete();
    xml = Regex.Replace(xml, "Target=\"mailto:[^\"]*\"", $"Target=\"{Target}\"");
    using var writer = new StreamWriter(zip.CreateEntry(RelsPath).Open(), new UTF8Encoding(false));
    writer.Write(xml);
}

static string ReadTarget(string path)
{
    using var zip = ZipFile.OpenRead(path);
    using var reader = new StreamReader(zip.GetEntry(RelsPath)!.Open());
    return Regex.Match(reader.ReadToEnd(), "Target=\"([^\"]*)\"").Groups[1].Value;
}
```

